' RSystemInfo (RapidR's): what this computer has, read here and never
' sent by RapidR. What it says differs from one computer to the next, so
' the case checks its shape: every fact there and in range, Class in plain
' words, Summary a sentence, FreeMemory read again each time, Refresh.
' The same on every runtime.
DIM Info AS RSystemInfo
DIM c AS STRING

IF Info.OS <> "" THEN PRINT "os: known"
IF Info.Cores > 0 THEN PRINT "cores: yes"
IF Info.TotalMemory > 0 THEN PRINT "memory: yes"
IF Info.FreeMemory > 0 AND Info.FreeMemory <= Info.TotalMemory THEN PRINT "free memory: within the total"
IF Info.DiskFree <= Info.DiskTotal THEN PRINT "disk: free within the size"
IF Info.BatteryLevel >= -1 AND Info.BatteryLevel <= 100 THEN PRINT "battery: in range"
IF Info.HasBattery <> 0 OR Info.OnBattery = 0 THEN PRINT "battery: consistent"
c = Info.Class
IF c = "small" OR c = "medium" OR c = "large" THEN PRINT "class: plain words"
IF RIGHT$(Info.Summary, 1) = "." THEN PRINT "summary: a sentence"
IF INSTR(Info.Summary, "cores") > 0 THEN PRINT "summary: says the cores"
IF Info.Unknown = "" THEN PRINT "unknown: nothing here"
IF Info.Browser = 0 THEN PRINT "browser: no"
IF Info.Refresh THEN PRINT "refreshed"
IF Info.Cores > 0 THEN PRINT "after refresh: cores again"
